     "html": "<p>Use partial quotients to divide. You may use counters or draw pictures to help.</p> <p><img src=\"assets/lessons/flfeg4t5l4en_section_2_sub_1_text_01.png\" alt=\"92 divided by 4.\"></p> <p>Ask: How many 4s are in 92? Try 20.</p> <p><span class=\"mth\">4 × 20 = 80</span>, and <span class=\"mth\">92 - 80 = 12</span> left.</p>  <p>Then: How many 4s are in 12? 3.</p> <p><span class=\"mth\">4 × 3 = 12</span>, so there is no remainder.</p>  <p>The partial quotients are 20 and 3.</p> <p>Add them to find the quotient: <span class=\"mth\">20 + 3 = 23</span>. </p> <p>So, <span class=\"mth\">92 ÷ 4 = 23</span>.</p>"
